	"description": [
		"Students learn about and analyze the English language, beginning with the building blocks of language: morphology, syntax, semantics, and phonetics/phonology. Students also explore the ways humans acquire language, social and geographical influences on English, and major changes during thehistory of the English language. The course serves as an introduction to the linguistic studies concentration, and fulfills the linguistics requirement of the Communication Arts and Literature license. Prerequisite: FYW."
